@nilsaggu Is that a joke? Cooling is the single most difficult problem in space stations, satellites, etc. Sending Data Centers to space is a tech bro myth, it will never be economical or reasonable.
Not just because all the intense radiation destroys the consumer grade electronics, not just because space hardened compute is over thirty years behind that of normal compute, not just because of the extreme cost of getting anything into space, not just because you need at least some techs on site to handle hardware issues, not just because we lack the means to get large enough structures built into space, not just because of the aforementioned heat management issues; but all of the above and more.

We need less Data Centers, it's that simple. Also Data Centers should have to build vertically.

